## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to implement a simple, offline-first persistence layer with Codable, basic CRUD in a SwiftUI app, and derive a user-facing metric (streak) from daily entries. It avoids external dependencies and targets beginner-friendly data modeling and UI work.

## Key Concepts
- SwiftUI, Codable, FileManager and Documents directory usage
- Data model design for Habit and DayEntry
- Derived metrics: computing daily streaks from consecutive entries
- Basic CRUD operations and crash-safe resume through persistent storage
- Lightweight test plan focusing on persistence and streak logic

## Code Example
```swift
struct DayEntry: Codable { let date: Date; let completed: Bool }
struct Habit: Codable { let id: UUID; var name: String; var colorHex: String; var entries: [DayEntry] }

let url = FileManager.default.urls(for: .documentDirectory, in: .userDomainMask).first!.appendingPathComponent("habits.json")
func save(_ habits: [Habit]) throws {
  let data = try JSONEncoder().encode(habits)
  try data.write(to: url)
}
func load() -> [Habit] {
  guard let data = try? Data(contentsOf: url) else { return [] }
  return (try? JSONDecoder().decode([Habit].self, from: data)) ?? []
}
```

